*.env
# `*.env` only matches names ENDING in .env, so a backup or variant like
# `.env.bak.1789747496`, `.env.save` or `.env.production` slipped through and could
# be committed with live keys in it. Match anything that starts with .env instead,
# then re-allow the placeholder template.
.env.*
!.env.example
